SUBGROUP PERFORMANCE ANALYSIS - EIGHT_FEATURES
================================================================================
Subgroup PERFORMANCE, not a fairness evaluation — see this module's docstring.

train: 1584 lab-event rows -> 425 patients, 327 events (patient-level event rate 0.7694)
test: 472 lab-event rows -> 107 patients, 82 events (patient-level event rate 0.7664)
IPCW censoring reference: the full training cohort (425 patients), not a per-group one; evaluation capped at 3164.4 days (training follow-up 3164.4 days).

Patient metadata join:
  107 held-out patients; 0 with no patients.csv row
  Age variable — anchor_age from patients.csv — the patient's age in their MIMIC anchor year, NOT their age at the prediction landmark; the exported scenario CSVs carry no absolute timestamp, so landmark age is not derivable here
  Time from each patient's first lab record to their prediction landmark: median 0.002 y, p90 1.436 y, max 7.262 y — the landmark can sit this far from the anchor year the age is measured at.
  Race — most frequently recorded race across the patient's admissions, ties broken by earliest admission; patients with no recorded value are kept as UNKNOWN/NOT RECORDED
    105/107 patients have a recorded race; 2 retained as unknown; 6 have more than one recorded value across admissions; 8 admission rows carry declined/unobtainable/unknown.
